tree trunk\ntd.line(P([(1048,590),(1054,500),(1042,438),(1058,360),(1040,300)]), fill=C('#6F5537'), width=Lw(9))\ntd.line(... highlight)\nbranches ...\n# canopy clusters list around (1010,330),(1060,290),(1085,360),(980,400), etc.\nfor cluster, draw 10 blobs with varying colors; add highlights\n# left shrub branches from x=480...\n# far hedge bottom as many small circles y 545-595\n# meadow grass strokes\n# wildflowers\n```\nNeed mask applied to all. Use `td` before mask. For highlights, can use same layer with lighter colors. Add specks as small ellipses. Then apply mask and comp blur 1.8. Then add dappled layer additional highlights (maybe keep existing dap but enhance).\n\nAvoid overly detailed at final size. Use 40-60 blobs. Let's write deterministic random with rnd.\n\nColors: deep green #5F764A, mid #748B56, light #8FA568, sunlit #B6BD78, golden #C9BE7C. Right tree canopy backlit: dark #536B45, #6F8652, #879B5E, highlights #C7C986. Left similar.\n\nSun at x 940,245: draw leaves overlapping sun after highlight: small branch with leaves across disc (x=880..1000 y=220..270). This adds depth.\n\nBranches dark silhouette in front of sun and sky. Use `td.line` with dark brown.\nStone wall at bottom: skip, maybe add a low wooden fence behind hedge at y=520? tiny.\nMeadow foreground: at y=575..592, draw vertical grass strokes in ochre/green, and 5 poppy dots in coral/cream. This adds detail near the sill.\nAdd soft haze overlay? not needed.\n\nLet's code replacement with Python using string indices. Use `python3` to replace substring between \"# trees, layered for depth\" and \"# two birds\". We'll include new block.\n\nNeed ensure no duplicate images after mask. Great.\n\nPot rack replacement: block from \"# rail\" to \"# dried herbs\" maybe. We'll write:\n```\n# rail, brackets\n...\ndef s_hook(x,y):\n  line from rail down, curve loop\n# hanging saucepan by angled handle\n# body position: x=1190..1280, y=320..390\n# handle from (1272,335) to (1310,255) then hook at 1310? wait hook separation\n```\nLet's design coordinates to fit:\nRail x=1178..1568 y=246.\nHook positions: 1230, 1340, 1462, 1540.\n1. Saucepan: hangs by handle from hook at 1230. Body center x=1245,y=360. Handle line from (1255,335) to (1235,278) diagonal up-left. Pan body: shape wider than tall: ellipse/rounded body x=1200..1300 y=325..385, flared rim ellipse x=1200..1300 y=315..340. Side helper handle on left: small arc loop at (1195,340). The pan hangs by the long handle so body shifts right of handle. Draw handle (thick dark metal with wood grip? copper). Use copper handle with dark outline; body copper. The handle attaches at rim right side (1270,335) and goes to hook (1233,272). It will cross body? okay.\n2. Skillet: hook at 1342, body center x=1390, y=370? Handle from body left (1345,350) up to hook 1342,270, diagonal. Body x=1330..1440 y=330..400, ellipse; interior dark. Hmm body would extend into clock area y<430 no issue. Handle from (1350,340) to (1338,274) short. Pan body to right.\n3. Colander: hook at 1462, body x=1420..1505 y=325..395; two loop handles; center hanging loop to hook? Use one small loop at top. Copper colander with holes. Use half-circle body: ellipse plus bottom; holes in rows. Add rim.\n4. Ladle: hook at 1522; long handle down to y=400, bowl at 1512,412; copper.\n5. Dried herbs at far right hook 1554? can overlap. Maybe remove herbs or hang at 1558. Rail ends 1568, small bundle.\n6. Clock at 1418,476 below rack; no overlap.\n\nCould simplify: saucepan + skillet + colander + herbs. Use hooks at 1235, 1345, 1460, 1540.\n\nNeed ensure visual distinction and not look like mugs. Draw pot bodies with flared rims and handles.\nSaucepan body spec:\n```\nbody=[(1198,332),(1205,360),(1214,378),(1245,384),(1276,376),(1288,354),(1289,334)]\ncatmull closed; fill copper; outline\nrim ellipse (1196,318,1292,344) fill lighter, inner ellipse dark\nhandle: line from (1278,330) to (1240,268), dark outline width 12, copper width 8, hook at 1238\n```\nActually handle attaches at rim and curves up to hook, so it would be on right top. Great.\nAdd two rivets.\nAdd highlight crescent and reflected warm light.\n3. Skillet: handle from (1370,335) up to (1340,268); body x=1320..1430 y=335..402 with dark interior; rim. \n4. Colander: body half sphere x=1435..1520 y=330..400, fill copper, rim ellipse at y=325..350, two loop handles at sides, holes: 20 dots in rows clipped? Draw dots only inside body roughly. Add feet? Hanging.\n5. Ladle maybe skip for space; add one wooden spoon hanging on far right instead of herbs? Herbs nice.\n6. A copper measuring cup? no.\n\nClock is too plain but fine. Add a small shelf under clock? no.\n\nNext, sunbeam and shadow improvements after scene. We can add more overlay passes before final grade:\n- soft shadows on wall under shelf and pot rack; draw after everything? If after, they'd cover shelf; shadows should be behind. We can add subtle shadows directly around/behind at end with low alpha, but they will overlay objects. Could use multiply blend on scene? A shadow overlay at alpha 10 over objects is not bad. Add soft shadow behind/under shelves and clock by drawing on overlay and comp after all (it will slightly darken shelf too). Better limited to wall gaps, but okay.\n- Directional shadows on counter: add ellipses to left of objects after the objects? That would overlay objects if not careful. Use polygons starting at object base extending left; draw before objects ideally. Existing call positions are before objects, but we can add additional ones before each object. Could use a global post-pass with soft polygons only in areas without objects? complicated. Existing shadows enough maybe.\n- Add slanted window light bands on cabinets and floor. Do post-pass with low alpha screen. \n- Add warm rim highlights on counter items at end (thin lines) to unify. e.g., on kettle, bowl, mugs, cat. Some already.\n\nMaybe a global lighting overlay can do a lot: a \"light\" layer with a polygon from window down-left, then use `ImageChops.screen` to brighten areas. Our comp with alpha just lightens. Increase alpha and add sharp rays. Add dust.\n\n- Add a gentle warm glow on the right side wall/cabinets near window? no.\n\n- Deepen shadows: add a final gradient vignette stronger at bottom, and cool tint in shadows. Current vi","truncated":true}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_00_NMzq4M0LBuSI0YSsmGiu7146","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/vellery-bmuf3gwh/work && python3 - <<'PY'\np='art/draw_kitchen.py'\ns=open(p).read()\n\nstart=s.index('# trees, layered for depth')\nend=s.index('# two birds')\nnew = '''# trees and garden, layered for depth\ntrees=newlayer(); td=ImageDraw.Draw(trees)\n\n# right-hand tree trunk and branches\ntrunk=[(1064,596),(1058,548),(1067,502),(1054,452),(1062,402),(1050,350),(1055,302)]\nfor w,col in [(13,'#5A422C'),(8,'#765538'),(3,'#9C7B50')]:\n    td.line(P(trunk), fill=C(col), width=Lw(w), joint='curve')\n# branches\nfor br in [[(1056,430),(1028,398),(995,382)],[(1056,392),(1082,360),(1104,338)],\n           [(1050,352),(1012,330),(980,322)],[(1060,490),(1088,468),(1107,440)],\n           [(1060,532),(1030,512),(1002,508)]]:\n    td.line(P(br), fill=C('#6A4B31'), width=Lw(5), joint='curve')\n    td.line(P(br), fill=C('#8C6844'), width=Lw(1.8), joint='curve')\n\n# leafy canopy clusters\ndef leaf_cluster(cx,cy,rx,ry,dark,mid,light,fruit=True):\n    td.ellipse(B(cx-rx,cy-ry,cx+rx,cy+ry), fill=C(dark,245))\n    for i in range(24):\n        a=rnd.uniform(0,math.tau); rad=rnd.uniform(0,1)**.55\n        ex=cx+math.cos(a)*rx*.82*rad; ey=cy+math.sin(a)*ry*.82*rad\n        rr=rnd.uniform(.14,.32)*rx\n        col=light if (ex>cx and ey<cy and rnd.random()<.7) else (mid if rnd.random()<.72 else dark)\n        td.ellipse(B(ex-rr,ey-rr*.72,ex+rr,ey+rr*.72), fill=C(col,230))\n    # sunlit edge dabs\n    for i in range(12):\n        ex=cx+rnd.uniform(-.25,.85)*rx; ey=cy-rnd.uniform(.1,.85)*ry\n        rr=rnd.uniform(2,6)\n        td.ellipse(B(ex-rr,ey-rr*.7,ex+rr,ey+rr*.7), fill=C('#D7D291',rnd.randint(110,205)))\n\nleaf_cluster(1015,315,112,88,'#536943','#718652','#91A466')\nleaf_cluster(960,392,82,76,'#5B7148','#788C58','#9AAA6C')\nleaf_cluster(1058,378,88,92,'#4E6541','#6A7F4D','#8FA467')\nleaf_cluster(1070,480,74,82,'#516943','#6E8552','#8FA468')\nleaf_cluster(995,505,60,54,'#5E7449','#7C9059','#A2B471')\nleaf_cluster(1100,442,48,55,'#5C7247','#7B8F57','#A8B474')\n# left side foliage\nleaf_cluster(492,342,72,88,'#566B45','#778C57','#9AAD6C')\nleaf_cluster(470,427,62,76,'#5C7248','#7A8F59','#A0B171')\nleaf_cluster(540,465,52,50,'#647A4D','#81965E','#ABB878')\n# low hedge across the garden\nfor i in range(20):\n    hx=452+i*32.5\n    hy=568+random.uniform(-8,7)\n    rr=random.uniform(19,30)\n    col=['#6F854F','#7F955B','#667C4A','#8CA063'][i%4]\n    td.ellipse(B(hx-rr,hy-rr*.72,hx+rr,hy+rr*.72), fill=C(col,235))\n    td.arc(B(hx-rr,hy-rr*.72,hx+rr,hy+rr*.72), 195, 315, fill=C('#B9BE80',90), width=Lw(2))\n# meadow grasses\nfor i in range(80):\n    gx=rnd.uniform(455,1085); gy=rnd.uniform(572,592)\n    td.line(P([(gx,gy),(gx+rnd.uniform(-5,5),gy-rnd.uniform(3,12))]),\n            fill=C(['#8C9B5D','#A9AF70','#778B50'][i%3],145), width=Lw(1))\n# wildflowers near the sill\nfor i in range(11):\n    fx=rnd.uniform(465,1080); fy=rnd.uniform(556,586)\n    td.line(P([(fx,fy+7),(fx+rnd.uniform(-2,2),fy-4)]), fill=C('#6D8650',170), width=Lw(1))\n    td.ellipse(B(fx-3,fy-7,fx+3,fy-1), fill=C(['#E9D8A7','#E6A07C','#F1E8CF'][i%3],220))\n    td.ellipse(B(fx-1,fy-5,fx+1,fy-3), fill=C('#C8914F',200))\n\ntrees.putalpha(ImageChops.multiply(trees.getchannel('A'),glass_mask))\ncomp(trees, blur=1.7)\n\n# foreground leaves crossing the sun, for depth\nfrontleaf=newlayer(); fld=ImageDraw.Draw(frontleaf)\nfld.line(P([(1074,300),(1022,282),(982,268),(948,258)]), fill=C('#5A422C'), width=Lw(3))\nfor i in range(12):\n    lx=945+i*11; ly=256+math.sin(i*.8)*5\n    fld.ellipse(B(lx-5,ly-3,lx+5,ly+3), fill=C(['#5F7548','#788C55','#8FA363'][i%3],220))\nfrontleaf.putalpha(ImageChops.multiply(frontleaf.getchannel('A'),glass_mask))\ncomp(frontleaf, blur=.8)\n\n# dappled leaf highlights\ndap=newlayer(); dd=ImageDraw.Draw(dap)\nfor i in range(95):\n    if i<42:\n        x=rnd.uniform(455,700); y=rnd.uniform(310,560)\n    else:\n        x=rnd.uniform(900,1090); y=rnd.uniform(300,560)\n    r=rnd.uniform(1.2,6.5)\n    dd.ellipse(B(x-r,y-r*.7,x+r,y+r*.7), fill=C('#E8E2A8',rnd.randint(22,70)))\n# a few bright glints in the left canopy\nfor x,y in [(505,300),(525,330),(475,370),(1000,290),(1030,330),(1050,420)]:\n    dd.ellipse(B(x-7,y-3,x+7,y+3), fill=C('#F2E7B0',45))\ndap.putalpha(ImageChops.multiply(dap.getchannel('A'),glass_mask))\ncomp(dap)\n\n'''\ns=s[:start]+new+s[end:]\n\n# ---- replace pot rack block ----\nstart=s.index('# rail\\nD.line(P([(1178,246),(1568,246)])')\nend=s.index('# clock\\nccx,ccy=1418,476')\nnew='''# rail\nD.line(P([(1178,246),(1568,246)]), fill=C('#3D3027'), width=Lw(6))\nD.line(P([(1180,243),(1566,243)]), fill=C('#9A8166'), width=Lw(1.2))\nfor bx in (1206,1542):\n    D.line(P([(bx,246),(bx,220)]), fill=C('#3D3027'), width=Lw(4))\n    D.rectangle(B(bx-10,216,bx+10,225), fill=C('#4A392C'))\n    D.ellipse(B(bx-4,221,bx+4,229), fill=C('#8E7358'))\n\ndef pot_hook(x, tip_y):\n    # little S hook with a loop\n    pts=catmull([(x,247),(x,262),(x+4,273),(x,283)],samples=10)\n    D.line(P(pts), fill=C('#46372A'), width=Lw(2.6), joint='curve')\n    D.arc(B(x-6,tip_y-2,x+6,tip_y+11), 180, 360, fill=C('#46372A'), width=Lw(2.3))\n\n# copper saucepan, hung by its handle\npot_hook(1232,270)\nD.line(P([(1276,335),(1262,314),(1248,294),(1235,277)]), fill=C('#4A3424'), width=Lw(10), joint='curve')\nD.line(P([(1276,335),(1262,314),(1248,294),(1235,277)]), fill=C('#A86A42'), width=Lw(5.2), joint='curve')\nD.ellipse(B(1232,279,1246,293), fill=C('#5B3A26'))\nbody=[(1197,335),(1200,355),(1209,374),(1228,383),(1253,384),(1276,375),(1288,357),(1291,335)]\nbody=catmull(body,closed=True,samples=12)\nD.polygon(P(body), fill=C('#B9683F'))\nD.line(P(body+[body[0]]), fill=C('#5B3422'), width=Lw(2), joint='curve')\nD.ellipse(B(1195,318,1293,347), fill=C('#C77A4C'), outline=C('#5B3422'), width=Lw(1.8))\nD.ellipse(B(1204,324,1284,342), fill=C('#7B402C'))\nD.arc(B(1200,329,1288,387), 15, 165, fill=C('#F0AC74'), width=Lw(2.2))\nD.arc(B(1206,340,1270,390), 110, 245, fill=C('#F9C58D'), width=Lw(6))\nD.line(P([(1203,351),(1203,373)]), fill=C('#FFE0B4',100), width=Lw(2))\n# helper handle\nD.arc(B(1182,336,1206,360), 280, 110, fill=C('#5B3422'), width=Lw(5))\nD.arc(B(1184,338,1204,358), 280, 110, fill=C('#B9683F'), width=Lw(2.2))\nD.ellipse(B(1270,329,1282,339), fill=C('#E4A16D'))\n# skillet\npot_hook(1344,270)\nD.line(P([(1372,338),(1364,315),(1352,292),(1346,276)]), fill=C('#4A3424'), width=Lw(9), joint='curve')\nD.line(P([(1372,338),(1364,315),(1352,292),(1346,276)]), fill=C('#A86A42'), width=Lw(4.5), joint='curve')\nD.ellipse(B(1315,334,1435,403), fill=C('#B25F3B'), outline=C('#5A3322'), width=Lw(2))\nD.ellipse(B(1324,337,1427,381), fill=C('#C17549'))\nD.ellipse(B(1332,344,1419,373), fill=C('#66392A'))\nD.arc(B(1318,357,1432,402), 12, 168, fill=C('#EEA66E'), width=Lw(2.4))\nD.arc(B(1324,342,1428,392), 190, 300, fill=C('#F8C48B',120), width=Lw(5))\nD.ellipse(B(1323,331,1341,343), fill=C('#D68A58'))\n# copper colander\npot_hook(1462,270)\nD.line(P([(1462,280),(1462,296)]), fill=C('#46372A'), width=Lw(3))\nD.ellipse(B(1418,324,1522,390), fill=C('#B8663E'), outline=C('#5A3322'), width=Lw(2))\nD.ellipse(B(1413,315,1527,345), fill=C('#C97C4D'), outline=C('#5A3322'), width=Lw(1.8))\nD.ellipse(B(1423,321,1517,340), fill=C('#7B402C'))\nD.arc(B(1422,337,1518,392), 10, 170, fill=C('#F0AC74'), width=Lw(2.2))\nD.arc(B(1424,340,1490,392), 110, 240, fill=C('#F7C088'), width=Lw(5))\nfor r in range(3):\n    for c in range(7):\n        hx=1437+c*11; hy=350+r*10\n        if (hx-1470)**2/900 + (hy-358)**2/210 < 1:\n            D.ellipse(B(hx-2,hy-2,hx+2,hy+2), fill=C('#5E3424'))\n# colander loop handles\nD.arc(B(1402,337,1424,357), 260, 100, fill=C('#5A3322'), width=Lw(4.5))\nD.arc(B(1516,337,1538,357), 260, 100, fill=C('#5A3322'), width=Lw(4.5))\n# ladle at far right\npot_hook(1544,282)\nD.line(P([(1544,290),(1544,384)]), fill=C('#473628'), width=Lw(4))\nD.line(P([(1544,290),(1544,384)]), fill=C('#A86A42'), width=Lw(2.2))\nD.ellipse(B(1