wever cat's head at (1040..1130) and body starts 1088; collar would be hidden. Could place at neck where head meets body, lower right of head, visible. Add a small dusty red band and bell; adds charm.\n- Add more pronounced stripes and fur tufts.\n- Tail rings as thick dark orange bands; okay.\n- Add a tiny smile? sleeping.\n\nStool:\nCoordinates:\n- shadow soft polygon (110,1140)...\n- Draw after rug? Stool is left of rug, no overlap. Insert before slippers.\n- legs: back center leg (208,1028)-(220,1110) dark; front legs (152,1035)-(122,1130) and (272,1035)-(306,1140) with thickness 10.\n- cross rungs at x=140..290 y=1085, curved.\n- seat: ellipse (130,1004,300,1042), fill wood; side band rounded rect y=1025..1048.\n- folded throw: polygon on seat x=150..280 y=980..1032, cream with terracotta stripes, draped over front edge to y=1065. Maybe too tall but adds coziness. \n- Add a small sprig or a book on top? With throw folded, add a small book on top? Might be busy. Add a small ceramic bowl? no.\n- Folded blanket in dusty blue + cream stripes to echo cushion; draw 2 stacked folds. A knitted throw with fringe hanging.\n- Stool could be positioned near the bowl of oranges, implying someone about to sit. Nice.\n- Slippers in front maybe overlap leg, fine.\n- Add a small tin bucket under stool? no.\n- Ensure stool not hide slippers too much.\n\nSunlight:\n- Add a warm patch on stool/floor left from window. Beam overlay after all.\n- Steam boost and shadows.\n\nLet's code these changes."}
