cat on windowsill? no, already cat.\n\nLet's focus on lighting/atmosphere, which is what elevates. Need simulate morning beams:\n- Add a soft golden light gradient across the room from window to lower left. The existing beam comps are too subtle. Increase:\n  - broad warm beam from window bottom-left: polygon (450,126)-(700,126)-(430,1200)-(120,1200), alpha 22 warm; blur 40. This will warm the left side including cabinets/stool, creating a diagonal.\n  - narrower visible sun rays: 3 polygons from between mullions to left floor, alpha 12-18, blur 14. These overlay objects and create atmosphere.\n  - maybe add a strong floor sun pool left of rug and a warm rim on the stool.\n- Add cool shadow wash on right side to contrast: subtle blue-gray overlay at right top corner/cabinets, alpha 8.\n- Add projected window light on countertop with warm alpha 70, plus dark muntin shadows. Current pane patches barely visible. Increase alpha to 50 and add dark strips.\n- Add long shadows under objects: add elongated soft polygons after objects? We can add an overlay blended with multiply at low alpha, but this will darken object bases. Instead add manually to shadow positions in code? too many. Could add a global soft shadow layer under objects at the start; but each object already has an ellipse. The shadows are there but subtle. Increase floor/counter shadows maybe by adding at end with `ImageChops.multiply` and mask. Maybe easier: at final, compute a \"shadow\" overlay from contact points? no.\n\n- Add atmospheric glow around window: a large soft yellow radial behind curtains, using screen mode. We can overlay with rgba alpha 20 and blur 80. \n- Add a bright sunlight streak on the floor: a broad diagonal from window across rug? Rug in floor. Draw warm light over rug at alpha 30 with a distinct window pane shape. The cat should sit in a sunbeam, so its top rim glows. Add light polygons on the rug crossing cat, but if drawn after cat, it will wash the cat. Low alpha 18 okay. This gives \"sleeping in sun\" feel.\n- Add dust motes in the beams larger and more visible.\n\nDo a post-pass before final grade:\n```\n# warm atmospheric sun rays\nrays layer...\npolygons for 4 rays with alpha 10-20\ncomp blur 30\n# localized glow at window\nsoft_ellipse 780,360,600,450 C('#FFDCA0') alpha 20 blur 60 (but overlaps scene, wash)\n# floor sunbeams\ncomp blur 10\n# darken right side slightly with blue shadow\n```\nMake sure not too yellow. The palette is already warm brown; more golden could make it sepia. Add cool lavender/blue in shadows to balance. \nUse shadow tint #3A4E5C with low alpha 10 in right corners and under counter. \nAdd a warm light edge along left sides of objects? Light from window behind/above means front edges in shadow, but stylized.\n\nMaybe better to adjust final color grading: increase contrast and warmth of highlights, cool shadows. Current output is low contrast and fairly flat. Let's implement final color grade:\n- After downscale, create lum mask.\n- Shadows: overlay #2E3B4A alpha up to 45 based on darkness; but this will make dark areas blue rather than black. Add.\n- Highlights: overlay #FFD79B alpha up to 25 on light areas. \n- Add a subtle warm-to-cool gradient (left warm, right cool?) Window center. \n- Increase contrast 1.06, saturation 1.05, brightness slightly.\n- Add a soft bloom around window: extract highlights, blur, screen. `bloom = out.filter(GaussianBlur(20)); ImageChops.screen(out, bloom*0.15)`. But high-res 1600x1200, okay. Highlights near window/sun bloom. Use a mask from bright pixels. This will add morning glow. Do:\n```\nlum = out.convert('L')\nbright = lum.point(lambda v: max(0, v-190)*1.5)\nblur = out.filter(GaussianBlur(18))\nbloom_layer = Image.composite(blur, black, bright)\nout = ImageChops.screen(out, bloom_layer.point(lambda v:int(v*0.35)))\n```\nNeed careful not to overexpose. Sun/window brightest; nice.\n- Add warm glow around lamps? no.\n\nLet's also improve steam (stronger) and maybe add a faint sunlit dust. Current steam almost invisible. Increase alpha and add shadow lines.\n- Replace steam block. Use soft thicker wisps:\n```\nsteam layer:\nfor main kettle 2 ribbons from spout (1136,618) up to 500/430:\n  pts catmull with curls\n  line alpha 115, width 6, blur 2\n  line alpha 55 width 12 blur 6\n  maybe add a warm shadow line offset +2 alpha 30.\nmug steam alpha 80.\n```\nDraw both sharp and soft; after comp, add a warm glow behind? Good.\n- Current steam white on light wall almost invisible. Use pale cream with slight warm shadow. It will show. Or gray-blue steam shadow with white highlight. Draw shadow (#9A8268, alpha 50) offset 2, then white 110. This adds visibility.\n\nPot rack wall shadow: add soft shadow behind/around rail at x=1180..1570 y=235..410 using an overlay? It should be behind pots, so add before rack, but after wall. We can edit block to add `soft_poly` before rail? Since soft functions composite immediately and current code draws rail after, add at start of rack block:\n```\nsoft_poly([(1185,250),(1560,250),(1550,410),(1195,410)], warm gray, 14, 18)\nsoft_ellipse(... under rail)\n```\nBut it will be a broad shadow behind pots. Good.\n- Similar for shelves and frame: add broad soft shadow on wall behind/under. Current shelf has soft shadow ellipse at y+22. Add thin shadow to the right under shelf? Light from top-right, shadow to left/down. \n- Clock shadow exists.\n\nWindow curtain folds are very flat; add blue-gray shadow inside folds maybe. They look okay.\n- Curtains could get sunlit edges (warm) to emphasize light. Add a highlight along inner edges and bottom. On left inner edge x=455, on right x=1080. Add line #FFF3D8 alpha 80. They already have a highlight at outer? Add.\n- Add curtain hems (bottom band) maybe.\n\nBowl of oranges: highlight with sun. fine.\n- Add a small steam over the bread? no.\n\nSink: add a few water droplets and a sponge. Good detail. Let's add a sponge near sink left (x=606..640, y=690..706) and a couple of drops on counter. But the soap bottle is at 568..604; sink at 636. Space 604..636: 32 px. A small sponge can sit at x=606..632. Add yellow-green sponge rectangle with holes. It would be in front of sink rim? fine. Adds realism. Also a small folded cloth at right of sink? no.\n- Add a wet glass? no.\n\nBread: add a small knife wit","truncated":true}
