{"type":"thinking","text":"Slippers look much better (though maybe like little brown shoes). Stool's blanket no cup is cleaner. Cat no collar. Cushion blue visible. Good.\n\nStill flat lighting. Need apply final atmosphere. Also the pot rack still weird connections. Maybe okay but can improve. The right wall clock is below pots, balanced. The scene has a small issue: the far right wall bracket at 1542 extends to top and the rail extends 1568, leaving a tiny bit; okay.\n\nThe image reads cozy morning well. Could stop here, but let's elevate with light and details. The overall palette is muted and warm; the window is luminous. A bit of bloom will help.\n\nLet's design the light pass and final grade carefully, ensuring no washing out.\n\nWe'll replace the LIGHT block from \"# window light beams sweeping\" to \"# dust motes\" maybe. And adjust final grade.\n\nNew light block:\n\n```\n# broad morning rays\nbeam = ...\n# 4 shafts:\npolygons:\n[(520,126),(680,126),(360,1200),(90,1200)] alpha 18\n[(690,126),(790,126),(600,1200),(380,1200)] alpha 16\n[(900,126),(1010,126),(900,1200),(650,1200)] alpha 12\ncomp(beam, blur=32)\n# rim glow around window\nglow = newlayer; ellipse; comp(glow, blur=60)\n# projected panes on counter:\nfor quads alpha 50/42 etc.\n# strong floor sunlight:\nfloor_pool layer polygon with alpha 35; comp blur 20\n# bright sliver on left edges? \n```\n\nCareful: `soft_ellipse` at center window after everything will wash out window and objects, but low alpha.\n\nProjected window light on the counter should align with window and sun. Window is y 126-592, counter y 680; light falls on counter. Quads:\n- Left pane lower: x=700..790 y=684..752; right pane lower: x=800..1000. But sink/objects cover; overlay alpha 40. Fine.\n- Add dark muntin shadow bands at x=790..810 and y=735..750? Could be nice: a slightly dark band across lit counter. Use comp dark alpha 20.\n- Light patch on floor in front of sink: broad polygon from (350,978) to (850,978) expanding; alpha 35 warm; blur 30. Combined with pane stripes? Add 3 vertical bright stripes from x=420..820 at floor. \n- On rug/cat: add a warm patch from (700,1050) to (1180,1180), alpha 20; the cat catches sun.\n- Add long soft shadows under stool/slippers? They already have.\n\nSteam:\n- Draw with more contrast. Test.\n\nDust motes:\n- Make 70, some bigger. Add faint glowing circles. With bloom, nice.\n\nFinal grade:\nLet's write:\n```\n# before downscale maybe warm overlay\nwarm already\n...\nout=...\n# Bloom\nlum=out.convert('L')\nbright=lum.point(lambda v: max(0,int((v-200)*2.2)))\nblurred=out.filter(GaussianBlur(18))\nbloom=Image.composite(blurred, Image.new('RGB',(W,H),(0,0,0)), bright)\nout=ImageChops.screen(out, Image.eval(bloom, lambda v:int(v*0.35)))\n# tint shadows/highlights\ngray=out.convert('L')\nsh_mask=gray.point(lambda v: int(max(0,(150-v))/150*55))\ncool=Image.new('RGB',(W,H),(44,61,74))\ncool_blend=Image.blend(out,cool,0.22)\nout=Image.composite(cool_blend,out,sh_mask)\nhi_mask=gray.point(lambda v: int(max(0,(190-v?))...\n```\nFor highlights, v>200: mask = (v-195)/60*55.\nwarm_img=(255,221,172); blend 0.12.\nThen contrast 1.04, saturation 1.05.\n# Add a warm top light gradient? no.\n\nPotential issue: shadow mask based on gray includes dark outlines and cat, tinting them blue. That adds cool shadows. Keep low 0.12 blend.\n- Bloom might make white sink glow too much. Limit 0.2.\n- Add slight film grain after grade; already noise before downsample. The current noise is fine.\n\nMaybe add a subtle canvas texture? already.\n\nAlso temperature: current image is green/yellow. Cool shadows will improve depth.\n\nCurtains sunlit:\nAdd after curtains code:\n```\nD.line along inner edges with #FFF4D6 alpha 120 width 3\nD.line along bottom with shadow\n```\nWould make them glow. We can add to curtain block. Also add window light on curtains. \n- Left curtain inner edge near x=444; draw line points [(470,100),(456,180),(430,360),(448,520),(424,610)] fill #FFF3D4 alpha 70 width 4? On top of folds, subtle.\n- Right similarly.\n- Add bottom hem shadow.\n- Could add a blue-gray inner stripe for color: line near outer edge with #C9B79B.\nThe curtains currently look pale and flat. Add warm highlight on inner edges and cool shadows in folds. Let's do at end of curtain section:\n```\nD.line(P([(462,100),(450,200),(438,310),(444,420),(434,520),(430,608)]), fill=C('#FFF4D9',90), width=Lw(3))\n...\n```\nNeed ensure not on window glass. Fine.\n\nWindow sill herb plant looks nice.\n\nPot rack connection fix:\n- Add ring loops:\n  - after saucepan handle, draw `D.ellipse(B(1228,271,1244,287), outline=C('#4A3424'), width=Lw(2))` but the hook loop already there. If ring overlaps hook, okay.\n  - Remove dark blob at top? Currently `D.ellipse(B(1232,279,1246,293), fill=C('#5B3A26'))` looks like a knob at handle end. That's the connection but maybe too big. Change to a ring: `D.ellipse(B(1233,276,1249,292), fill=C('#C9A06B'), outline=..., width=2)` with center hole? Draw outer darker and inner wall color? But background varies. We can draw a copper ring with dark center: outer ellipse fill copper, inner ellipse fill dark. It would look like a hole. Use small 3px inner. \n  - For skillet similarly.\n  - Colander loop: add a metal loop between top and hook, visible:\n    `D.arc(B(1454,283,1470,299), 0, 360...)` maybe. Better use an ellipse ring.\n  - Ladle ring at top.\n- Add wall shadows behind rack:\n  `soft_poly([(1180,248),(1570,248),(1560,420),(1190,420)], #6E5740, 14, 20)` before rail. But this broad wash may look dirty. Use alpha 10. Also shadow under rail.\n- Could add small cast shadows of pots on wall offset left/down. Draw soft ellipses at pot positions before pots:\n   `soft_ellipse(1210,385,55,22, dark, 25,8)`, but it overlays wall behind. use low alpha.\nThis enhances depth.\n\nNeed ensure tools don't add too much. Let's implement light pass first, see.\n\nReplace light block. We'll use Python markers from \"# window light beams sweeping down-left toward the floor\" to \"# dust motes in the light\". Replace with new beams/pane/floor. Keep dust motes but adjust after.\n\nLet's write.\n\nBeam:\n```\n# window bloom / light haze\nsoft_ellipse(770,330,570,420,C('#FFD79B'),16,70)\n```\nBut soft_ellipse draws solid ellipse then blurs; edge gradient. Low alpha. Good.\n- Rays: draw polygons on layer with alpha 20, composite blur 30. \n- `pane` with warm alpha 55.\n- `floor_pool` broad patch alpha 32, blur 25, plus 4 stripes alpha 14, blur 8.\n- Add sunlit rim on rug/cat: after floor pool maybe.\n- Add a few light slashes on the wall to the left of window (projected light) perhaps. There is wall x 0..400; sunlight from window could hit left wall? Not physically, but aesthetically add a warm patch at x=0..400 y=200..600 alph 12. Maybe not.\n\nDust motes: modify count and alpha, add big bokeh.\n\nSteam replace with stronger:\n```\nsteam_shadow layer maybe\nfor each wisp:\n  sd.line fill #FFF9EA alpha 130 widths 7,4; and soft 12 alpha 45\n```\nThe current steam loops are short and near window, hard to see. Create longer wisps:\nKettle spout at (1136,618). Wisps rise to y=450, curl left:\npts [(1139,612),(1128,590),(1135,566),(1150,544),(1141,520),(1120,498),(1124,472),(1140,450)]\nand another offset. \nMug steam from (1344,638) to (1338,560).\nDraw shadow offset +2,+3 color #8E745C alpha 30, width 6; then white alpha 120 width 5; then highlight alpha 130 width 2. Use blur comp. \nDon't overdo. Maybe steam in front of window/wall; good.\n\nSteam can overlap pot rack? Kettle at x=1220, steam rises to y=450, left of clock; fine. Mug steam rises to y=560, can overlap window sill? mug at 1344, x outside window; fine.\n\nDust motes maybe 70.\n\nFinal grade:\n- after out created and downscale, do bloom/tints.\n- Keep existing warm wash/vignette/grain then enhance.\n- Add sun rays inside final? no.\n\nLet's implement."}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_00_XoGc4Xuf3yNhaBUDZcea5929","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/vellery-bmuf3gwh/work && python3 - <<'PY'\np='art/draw_kitchen.py'\ns=open(p).read()\n\n# Add warm highlights to curtain inner edges / hems\nmarker=\"# ============================================================\\n# TILE BACKSPLASH\"\nif marker not in s: raise SystemExit('tile marker missing')\ncurtain_light='''# sun catching the inner edges of the curtains\nD.line(P([(466,104),(456,190),(438,300),(444,392),(432,480),(442,548),(424,606)]), fill=C('#FFF4D6',95), width=Lw(3.2), joint='curve')\nD.line(P([(1086,104),(1076,190),(1094,300),(1088,392),(1100,480),(1090,548),(1116,606)]), fill=C('#FFF4D6',80), width=Lw(3), joint='curve')\nD.line(P([(400,608),(444,604),(430,612),(398,615)]), fill=C('#B69975',140), width=Lw(1.5))\nD.line(P([(1110,606),(1150,608),(1148,615),(1114,613)]), fill=C('#B69975',120), width=Lw(1.4))\nsoft_poly([(390,614),(470,610),(466,628),(392,632)], C('#4C3020'),25,4)\n\n'''\ns=s.replace(marker,curtain_light+marker)\n\n# Add rack wall shadow and connection rings / remove herbs, improve ladle\ns=s.replace(\"# rail\\nD.line(P([(1178,246),(1568,246)])\",\n\"\"\"# soft wall shadow behind the hanging copperware\nsoft_poly([(1184,252),(1558,252),(1548,414),(1200,418)], C('#725A43'), 12, 18)\nsoft_ellipse(1372,404,195,20,C('#6B533D'),18,14)\n# rail\nD.line(P([(1178,246),(1568,246)])\"\"\")\n\ns=s.replace(\"D.ellipse(B(1232,279,1246,293), fill=C('#5B3A26'))\",\n\"\"\"D.ellipse(B(1231,276,1249,294), fill=C('#C1915D'), outline=C('#4B3422'), width=Lw(1.3))\nD.ellipse(B(1236,281,1244,289), fill=C('#4A3424'))\"\"\")\n\n# skillet connection ring\ns=s.replace(\"D.ellipse(B(1323,331,1341,343), fill=C('#D68A58'))\",\n\"\"\"D.ellipse(B(1323,331,1341,343), fill=C('#D68A58'))\nD.ellipse(B(1337,269,1355,287), fill=C('#C1915D'), outline=C('#4B3422'), width=Lw(1.3))\nD.ellipse(B(1342,274,1350,282), fill=C('#4A3424'))\"\"\")\n\n# colander visible hanging ring and connection\ns=s.replace(\"D.line(P([(1462,280),(1462,296)]), fill=C('#46372A'), width=Lw(3))\",\n\"\"\"D.line(P([(1462,280),(1462,294)]), fill=C('#46372A'), width=Lw(3))\nD.ellipse(B(1452,289,1472,309), outline=C('#4B3422'), width=Lw(3.2))\nD.ellipse(B(1458,295,1466,303), fill=C('#6E5036'))\"\"\")\n\n# remove the dried herbs block to declutter far right\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"# sprig of dried herbs\nD.line(P([(1560,258),(1558,330)]), fill=C('#6A7D4E'), width=Lw(2))\nfor i in range(10):\n    yy=266+i*7\n    side=-1 if i%2 else 1\n    D.ellipse(B(1558+side*2-4,yy-2,1558+side*8+4,yy+3), fill=C(['#7E8E5B','#96A36D','#66794C'][i%3]))\n\n\"\"\",\"\")\n\n# ladle connection ring\ns=s.replace(\"D.ellipse(B(1532,382,1556,406), fill=C('#B8683F'), outline=C('#5A3322'), width=Lw(1.5))\",\n\"\"\"D.ellipse(B(1536,277,1552,293), outline=C('#4B3422'), width=Lw(2.8))\nD.ellipse(B(1532,382,1556,406), fill=C('#B8683F'), outline=C('#5A3322'), width=Lw(1.5))\"\"\")\n\n# Replace light block\nstart=s.index(\"# window light beams sweeping down-left toward the floor\")\nend=s.index(\"# dust motes in the light\")\nnew='''# broad window haze and morning shafts\nsoft_ellipse(772,336,592,420,C('#FFD79A'),14,70)\nbeam=newlayer(); bd=ImageDraw.Draw(beam)\nbd.polygon(P([(500,126),(672,126),(350,1200),(60,1200)]), fill=C('#FFDFA4',20))\nbd.polygon(P([(668,126),(800,126),(610,1200),(330,1200)]), fill=C('#FFE6B4',17))\nbd.polygon(P([(900,126),(1014,126),(1010,1200),(700,1200)]), fill=C('#FFE9BB',12))\nbd.polygon(P([(560,126),(610,126),(250,1200),(160,1200)]), fill=C('#FFF0CC',10))\ncomp(beam, blur=30)\n\n# projected window panes on the counter\npane=newlayer(); pd=ImageDraw.Draw(pane)\npd.polygon(P([(742,682),(864,682),(898,756),(764,756)]), fill=C('#FFE7B3',52))\npd.polygon(P([(878,682),(1000,682),(1048,756),(914,756)]), fill=C('#FFE7B3',43))\npd.polygon(P([(1014,682),(1090,682),(1148,756),(1064,756)]), fill=C('#FFE7B3',30))\n# muntin shadow across the pool of light\npd.polygon(P([(866,682),(880,682),(916,756),(900,756)]), fill=C('#7A5638',22))\ncomp(pane, blur=4.5)\n\n# sun pooling on the floor, with pane-shaped bands\nfloor_light=newlayer(); fd2=ImageDraw.Draw(floor_light)\nfd2.polygon(P([(250,978),(820,978),(1070,1200),(330,1200)]), fill=C('#FFD79B',36))\nfor x0,w in [(340,120),(480,120),(620,120),(760,120)]:\n    fd2.polygon(P([(x0,978),(x0+w,978),(x0+w+190,1200),(x0+120,1200)]), fill=C('#FFE4B2',20))\ncomp(floor_light, blur=18)\n# sunbeam falling across the rug and cat\nsoft_poly([(720,1040),(1010,1004),(1210,1174),(880,1200)], C('#FFD99F'), 22, 15)\nsoft_poly([(1040,1044),(1130,1036),(1210,1090),(1110,1104)], C('#FFE6B7'), 24, 10)\n\n'''\ns=s[:start]+new+s[end:]\n\n# Replace steam block\nstart=s.index(\"# steam from kettle\\nsteam=newlayer()\")\nend=s.index(\"# dust motes in the light\")\nnew='''# steam from the kettle\nsteam=newlayer(); sd=ImageDraw.Draw(steam)\nfor k in range(3):\n    pts=[(1139+k*4,612),(1127+k*8,590),(1136+k*7,566),(1152+k*9,542),\n         (1142+k*11,518),(1122+k*12,496),(1128+k*10,470),(1143+k*8,448)]\n    pts=catmull(pts,samples=14)\n    # warm shadow\n    sd.line(P([(x+2,y+3) for x,y in pts]), fill=C('#9C8068',38), width=Lw(7-k*1.2), joint='curve')\n    sd.line(P(pts), fill=C('#FFF9EA',105-k*18), width=Lw(5.2-k*.9), joint='curve')\n    sd.line(P(pts), fill=C('#FFFDF5',125-k*20), width=Lw(1.6), joint='curve')\n# steam from the cream mug\nfor k in range(2):\n    pts=catmull([(1344+k*7,638),(1337+k*8,620),(1348+k*7,602),(1341+k*8,582),(1350+k*7,558),(1344+k*6,538)],samples=14)\n    sd.line(P([(x+1,y+2) for x,y in pts]), fill=C('#9C8068',30), width=Lw(5), joint='curve')\n    sd.line(P(pts), fill=C('#FFF9EA',80-k*20), width=Lw(3.4-k*.8), joint='curve')\ncomp(steam, blur=2.2)\n# a softer atmospheric halo around the steam\ncomp(steam, blur=10)\n\n'''\ns=s[:start]+new+s[end:]\n\n# Enhance dust motes block\nstart=s.index(\"# dust motes in the light\\nmotes=newlayer()\")\nend=s.index(\"# ============================================================\\n# FINAL GRADE\")\nnew='''# dust motes floating in the sun\nmotes=newlayer(); md2=ImageDraw.Draw(motes)\nfor i in range(78):\n    x=random.uniform(380,1150); y=random.uniform(260,1080)\n    r=random.uniform(.8,3.8)\n    a=random.randint(35,135)\n    md2.ellipse(B(x-r,y-r,x+r,y+r), fill=C('#FFEBC2',a))\nfor x,y,r in [(892,470,8),(764,692,6),(620,862,9),(1012,610,7),(520,930,5),(1110,760,4),(970,1110,5)]:\n    md2.ellipse(B(x-r,y-r,x+r,y+r), fill=C('#FFE7B0',20))\ncomp(motes, blur=1.2)\nfor x,y,r in [(892,470,6),(764,692,4),(620,862,7)]:\n    D.ellipse(B(x-r,y-r,x+r,y+r), outline=C('#FFE9BA',35), width=Lw(1.2))\n\n'''\ns=s[:start]+new+s[end:]\n\n# Final grade: bloom + split tone\nold='''out=canvas.convert('RGB').resize((W,H),Image.LANCZOS)\nout=out.filter(ImageFilter.UnsharpMask(radius=1.3, percent=80, threshold=3))\nout=ImageEnhance.Contrast(out).enhance(1.025)\nout=ImageEnhance.Color(out).enhance(1.035)\nout.save('/tmp/vellery-bmuf3gwh/work/art/cozy-kitchen-morning.png')\nout.save('/tmp/vellery-bmuf3gwh/work/art/cozy-kitchen-morning.jpg',quality=94)\nprint('saved',out.size)'''\nnew='''out=canvas.convert('RGB').resize((W,H),Image.LANCZOS)\nout=out.filter(ImageFilter.UnsharpMask(radius=1.25, percent=75, threshold=3))\n\n# gentle morning bloom from the window and bright copper\nlum=out.convert('L')\nbright=lum.point(lambda v: max(0,int((v-198)*2.0)))\nblurred=out.filter(ImageFilter.GaussianBlur(16))\nbloom=Image.composite(blurred,Image.new('RGB',(W,H),(0,0,0)),bright)\nbloom=ImageEnhance.Brightness(bloom).enhance(.62)\nout=ImageChops.screen(out,bloom)\n\n# cool shadows and warm highlights (split toning)\ngray=out.convert('L')\nshadow_mask=gray.point(lambda v:int(max(0,(142-v))/142*52))\ncool=Image.new('RGB',(W,H),(48,63,72))\ncoolblend=Image.blend(out,cool,.20)\nout=Image.composite(coolblend,out,shadow_mask)\ngray=out.convert('L')\nhi_mask=gray.point(lambda v:int(max(0,(200-v*0+0)) if False else max(0,(v-194))/.60*34))\nwarm=Image.new('RGB',(W,H),(255,221,170))\nwarmblend=Image.blend(out,warm,.15)\nout=Image.composite(warmblend,out,hi_mask)\n\nout=ImageEnhance.Contrast(out).enhance(1.06)\nout=ImageEnhance.Color(out).enhance(1.055)\nout=ImageEnhance.Brightness(out).enhance(1.005)\nout.save('/tmp/vellery-bmuf3gwh/work/art/cozy-kitchen-morning.png')\nout.save('/tmp/vellery-bmuf3gwh/work/art/cozy-kitchen-morning.jpg',quality=94)\nprint('saved',out.size)'''\nif old not in s: raise SystemExit('final block missing')\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint('patched light and grade')\nPY","description":"Add morning light, steam and color grade","timeoutMs":300000},"truncated":true}
